| Term                                     | Definition                                                                                                                           | Example                                                  |
| ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------- |
| **AI (Artificial Intelligence)**         | The broad field of creating systems that perform tasks requiring human intelligence.                                                 | ChatGPT, self-driving cars                               |
| **ML (Machine Learning)**                | A subset of AI where models learn patterns from data.                                                                                | Spam detection                                           |
| **DL (Deep Learning)**                   | A subset of ML using neural networks with many layers.                                                                               | Image recognition                                        |
| **LLM (Large Language Model)**           | A neural network trained on massive amounts of text to understand and generate language.                                             | GPT-5, Llama, Gemini                                     |
| **SLM (Small Language Model)**           | A compact language model optimized for speed and lower resource usage.                                                               | Phi, Gemma 3n                                            |
| **Prompt**                               | The input or instruction given to an LLM.                                                                                            | "Explain MVVM in Android."                               |
| **Prompt Engineering**                   | Designing prompts to get better responses from an AI model.                                                                          | Using role, context, examples                            |
| **Token**                                | The smallest unit an LLM processes (word or part of a word).                                                                         | "Android Developer" ≈ 2–3 tokens                         |
| **Context Window**                       | The maximum number of tokens the model can consider in one conversation.                                                             | 128K-token context window                                |
| **Embedding**                            | A numerical vector representation of text that captures its meaning.                                                                 | Used for semantic search                                 |
| **Vector Database**                      | Stores embeddings for similarity search.                                                                                             | Pinecone, Milvus, Chroma, FAISS                          |
| **RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation)** | Retrieves relevant information from an external knowledge base before generating an answer.                                          | Company chatbot searching internal documents             |
| **Fine-tuning**                          | Further training an LLM on domain-specific data.                                                                                     | Training on banking documents                            |
| **Inference**                            | Running a trained model to generate predictions or responses.                                                                        | ChatGPT answering your question                          |
| **Hallucination**                        | When an AI confidently generates incorrect or fabricated information.                                                                | Making up a non-existent API                             |
| **Temperature**                          | Controls randomness in generated text. Lower = deterministic, higher = creative.                                                     | 0.2 vs 1.0                                               |
| **Top-k / Top-p**                        | Sampling methods that control which next-token candidates the model can choose from.                                                 | Improves generation quality                              |
| **Agent**                                | An AI system that can reason, plan, use tools, and perform multi-step tasks.                                                         | AI travel planner                                        |
| **Tool Calling / Function Calling**      | Lets an LLM invoke external APIs or functions.                                                                                       | Booking a flight through an API                          |
| **MCP (Model Context Protocol)**         | A standard protocol that allows AI models to securely connect to external tools, databases, files, and services in a consistent way. | ChatGPT accessing GitHub or a database via an MCP server |
| **API**                                  | An interface that lets applications communicate with AI models.                                                                      | OpenAI API                                               |
| **Multimodal AI**                        | AI that understands multiple data types such as text, images, audio, and video.                                                      | Uploading a screenshot to ChatGPT                        |
| **Transformer**                          | The neural network architecture behind modern LLMs, using self-attention to understand relationships between tokens.                 | GPT, BERT, Llama                                         |
| **Attention Mechanism**                  | Helps the model focus on the most relevant parts of the input when generating output.                                                | Understanding long paragraphs                            |



